# Line endings. This repo is authored on Windows and runs in a Linux container.
#
# A CRLF that reaches the container is not a cosmetic problem: `#!/usr/bin/bash\r`
# makes the kernel look for an interpreter literally named "bash\r", which fails
# with "no such file or directory" naming a file that plainly exists. That
# presents on Fly as a crash loop with nothing in the logs pointing at the cause
# -- the same shape as the `wait -n` bug in tasks/lessons.md.
#
# Normalise everything to LF in the repository, and force LF in the working tree
# for anything an interpreter reads by its first line.

* text=auto

*.sh    text eol=lf
*.bash  text eol=lf
Dockerfile      text eol=lf
docker/*        text eol=lf
*.py    text eol=lf
*.sql   text eol=lf
*.yml   text eol=lf
*.yaml  text eol=lf
*.toml  text eol=lf

# Captured API payloads are the wire-format contract. Diffing them is rarely
# useful and they must never be munged.
tests/fixtures/*.json  -text -diff
